{title: 478 - Sweet Hour of Prayer}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C/G]Sweet hour of prayer Sweet hour of prayer [F]That calls me from [C]a world of care
[G]And bids me at [C]my Father's throne [F]Make all my wants [C]and wishes known
[C/G]In seasons of [G7/D]distress [Em]and [C]grief My soul [G7/D]has often [C/G]found relief
[C]And oft escaped [F]the tempter's [C]snare By Thy return, sweet hour of prayer

Verse 2:
[C/G]Sweet hour of prayer! [F]sweet hour [C]of prayer!
[C/G]thy wings shall my [F]petition [C]bear
[G]to him [C]whose truth [F]and faithfulness
[G]engage [C]the waiting [F]soul [C]to bless.
[C/G]And since [G7/D]he [Em]bids [C]me [G7/D]seek [Em]his [C/G]face,
[C/G]believe [G7/D]his [Em]word, [C]and [G7/D]trust [Em]his [C/G]grace,
[C]I'll cast [F]on him [C]my every care,
[C]and wait [F]for thee, [C]sweet hour of prayer!

Verse 3:
[C/G]Sweet hour of prayer! [F]sweet hour [C]of prayer!
[C/G]May I thy consolation share
[G]Till from [C]Mount Pisgah's [F]lofty [C]height
[G]I view [C]my home [F]and take [C]my flight.
[C/G]In my [G7/D]immortal flesh [Em]I'll [C/G]rise
[C/G]To size [G7/D]the [Em]everlasting [C/G]prize.
[C]And shout [F]while [C]passing through the air,
[C]"Farewell, [F]farewell, [C]sweet hour of prayer!"
